name issue_12_lossbwe_policer
describe Policer: 1.5 Mbps enforced by dropping, no queueing (queue=5ms); the loss-based estimate must keep backing off (#12)
# LossBasedBweV2 as libwebrtc ships it (cc v2): loss above the inherent level at a rate above the
# loss-limited bandwidth limits the target; the instant upper bound is 100 kbps / (loss - 5 %).
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=5ms
# 5 seeds (cc v2): net.loss_pct 7.7-9.9, freeze_total_ms 0-764, target 400-412 kbps. `cc v1`: loss 19.8-25.0, freezes 1.0-1.6 s.
expect net.loss_pct < 12
# Was < 1500. Owner sign-off on PR #186 (program.md 0.2, 2026-10-20 18:37 UTC): libwebrtc 10663 ms (10 seeds), ours 1777 on seed 1.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 2500
expect audio.interruptions <= 3
